      "summary": {
        "headline": "Transactions mail received per household: long-term change in the published values, FY2003 to FY2023.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "Transactions mail received per household (pieces per household per year) went from 275.6 in FY2003 to 114.4 in FY2023: it fell by 161.2 (58.5%) over the period. Since FY2018 (five years earlier) it fell by 31.2 (21.4%). Since FY2013 (ten years earlier) it fell by 104.0 (47.6%).",
            "metric": "transactions-received-per-household",
            "years": [
              2003,
              2023,
              2018,
              2013
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By income in FY2023, Transactions mail received per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for $65K to $100K at 130.0 and lowest for Under $35K at 72.8.",
            "metric": "transactions-received-per-household",
            "years": [
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By age in FY2023, Transactions mail received per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for Over 55 at 145.6 and lowest for Under 35 at 57.2.",
            "metric": "transactions-received-per-household",
            "years": [
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By education in FY2023, Transactions mail received per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for High school graduate at 124.8 and lowest for Less than high school at 98.8.",
            "metric": "transactions-received-per-household",
            "years": [
              2023
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "No projection is shown for Transactions mail received per household: Projections need at least 8 consecutive annual values; this series has fewer, so none is shown.",
          "Transactions mail received per household has no published value for some years in between, so gaps are left as gaps.",
          "Methodology change in FY2010: Diary data restated with new weighting. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2012: Correspondence/transactions split reclassified (FY2012 report). Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2013: Transactions restated: 2011 questionnaire (FY2013 report). Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2014: Weighting by home ownership (household-group tables). Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2015: Correspondence/transactions split reclassified (FY2015 report). Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2017: Correspondence/transactions split reclassified (FY2017 report). Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Household-group bands (age, income, education) were redefined over time, so group comparisons across years should be read with the methodology notes."
        ]
